DuskClient — GPL-3.0-or-later (see fabric.mod.json).

The cosmetics package (dev.fasterlauncher.client.cosmetics and
mixin/cosmetics) reimplements the on-the-wire and on-screen behaviour of
two projects so that Dusk players are interoperable with them:

- MinecraftCapes mod — https://github.com/MinecraftCapes/minecraftcapes-mod
  LGPL-2.1. Replicated: the profile API contract (api.minecraftcapes.net),
  the offline-UUID resolution rule, the on-disk cache layout
  (<type>/<hash[0:2]>/<hash>), the animated-cape frame rule
  (height != width/2 -> frames of width/2 rows, 100 ms each), the static
  cape padding rule, the 14x7 ears model UVs and the cape render types.
  No source files were copied.

- cosmetica-core — https://github.com/Cosmetica-cc/cosmetica-core
  Apache-2.0 (Isaiah "Eyezah" Meek, Mekal "Valoeghese" Covic et al.).
  Replicated: the PlayerSkin substitution approach for capes/elytra, and
  the accessory model format and placement rules described in
  docs/COSMETICS.md §1.2 — the block-model face/corner/UV conventions of
  CosmeticaModel and BlockFaceUV (cosmetics/model/AccessoryModel.java) and
  the attachment transform chain of Accessory.attachmentTransform /
  CosmeticaModel.submitOnPart (cosmetics/AccessoriesLayer.java), so that
  models authored for Cosmetica render in the same place here. The
  launcher's preview (launcher/src/lib/accessoryMesh.ts) bakes the same
  rules. No source files were copied.

The media package (dev.dusk.client.media and mixin/media) records and plays
back sessions the way ReplayMod does:

- ReplayMod — https://github.com/ReplayMod/ReplayMod
  GPL-3.0 (johni0702 et al.). Replicated: the .mcpr file format (a zip of
  metaData.json, recording.tmcpr as [int time][int length][packet] records
  and thumb), the capture point (every clientbound packet as the connection
  reads it, plus synthesized packets for the recording player's own
  entity), and playback through a serverless connection fed on the client
  thread, with backward seeks replaying from the start. Opening Dusk
  files in ReplayMod itself is untested. No source files were copied;
  the rolling clip buffer, the replay filter and all UI are Dusk's own.

Bundled cosmetics (src/main/resources/assets/duskclient/cosmetics) are
community capes and one Cosmetica accessory ("Red Fire Arm", cosmetica
id ufa1T) imported with tools/import_cosmetics.py; they are content, not
code, and are not covered by the licences above.

